# What EAS Build must NOT upload. EAS archives the whole repo from this folder,
# and once this file exists it is used INSTEAD of every .gitignore, so anything
# that has to stay off EAS is listed here, even if a .gitignore already has it.
#
# Why it exists: mobile/.gitignore was not being applied to the upload, so the
# local mobile/android folder went up with every build. EAS then built from that
# stale folder and handed back a .tar.gz holding two APKs: the real release one
# and the *debug* one from this PC, which opens on the Expo dev launcher ("scan
# a QR code") instead of the app.

# Generated native projects: EAS runs `expo prebuild` itself from app.json.
/mobile/android
/mobile/ios

# Secrets. The Firebase *admin* key is a server credential; the app build only
# needs google-services.json, which stays.
splix-*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not needed to build the app.
/admin
/backend
/API.md
/README.md
.claude/
/mobile/%ProgramData%

# Dependencies, caches, build output.
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
*.log
